WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:02.210 --> 00:03.600
Gekkouga, Double Team!

00:11.630 --> 00:12.120
Don't flinch!

00:12.400 --> 00:13.350
Bullet Punch!

00:20.300 --> 00:21.130
Aerial Ace!

00:26.680 --> 00:27.670
He did it!

00:29.600 --> 00:30.490
All right!

00:31.890 --> 00:33.030
Are you all right, Hassam?

00:34.930 --> 00:36.030
Take a long rest.

00:38.520 --> 00:39.280
Thank you.

00:40.320 --> 00:42.320
Those fast movements and powerful moves...

00:42.670 --> 00:44.680
Your Gekkouga is strong.

00:46.310 --> 00:47.390
Thank you very much.

00:48.650 --> 00:49.800
That was excellent.

00:50.280 --> 00:54.210
Do you not think this was a good battle to prepare yourself for the Gym match at the Eisetsu Gym?

00:54.800 --> 00:55.330
Yeah.

00:55.820 --> 00:56.160
Satoshi,

00:56.790 --> 00:58.620
make sure to win this next Gym match!

00:59.060 --> 00:59.590
Sure!

00:59.980 --> 01:01.750
I'll get my eighth badge, no matter what!

01:03.480 --> 01:03.810
Huh?

01:05.230 --> 01:06.150
It has been a while.

01:06.770 --> 01:08.150
Have you been doing well?

01:08.720 --> 01:10.320
Oh, it's you, Shota!

01:15.290 --> 01:21.010
Rival Showdown!
Satoshi VS Shota!!

01:21.970 --> 01:31.820
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:21.970 --> 01:31.820
Z

01:22.260 --> 01:24.070
While they were visiting a town as they continued their journey, Satoshi and his friends...

01:24.570 --> 01:28.330
...reunited with Shota, who has a lot of respect for Satoshi.

01:29.500 --> 01:31.150
What, at the Eisetsu Gym?

01:31.580 --> 01:31.960
Yes.

01:32.390 --> 01:34.880
I got my eighth badge there.

01:35.160 --> 01:37.020
Oh, so you got your eighth already?

01:37.310 --> 01:37.670
Yes.

01:39.230 --> 01:40.260
Wow!

01:40.710 --> 01:42.400
That's amazing, Shota!

01:42.400 --> 01:43.610
Shota, you're so good!

01:44.150 --> 01:47.330
I still only have seven. You've passed me, Shota.

01:47.780 --> 01:50.260
When you showed me your badges a while ago,

01:50.630 --> 01:52.290
I felt a little frustrated.

01:53.320 --> 01:53.840
So...

01:54.320 --> 01:55.110
...I wanted to catch up to you.

01:55.410 --> 01:55.950
Desperately.

01:56.350 --> 01:57.100
I see...

01:58.420 --> 02:00.210
I'll make sure to complete my batch with the next match too!

02:00.730 --> 02:03.630
Shota, what type of Gym is the Eisetsu Gym?

02:04.140 --> 02:05.920
Eisetsu had Ice types.

02:06.150 --> 02:08.680
That means Water types have an advantage.

02:09.230 --> 02:11.080
In that case, I'll go with Gekkouga!

02:11.350 --> 02:13.480
It was able to fight on even ground with Carne-san, after all.

02:13.980 --> 02:14.270
What?

02:14.820 --> 02:16.230
You battled the Champion?

02:16.710 --> 02:19.570
Yeah, they went up against Mega Sirknight!

02:29.830 --> 02:33.910
During our battle with Carne-san, Gekkouga and I were fully able to become one.

02:34.410 --> 02:35.270
"One"?

02:35.700 --> 02:38.010
Like back when you fought me?

02:45.080 --> 02:46.770
No... It was like...

02:47.110 --> 02:48.510
...it felt more right.

02:50.390 --> 02:53.480
It had a super-sized Water Shuriken on its back!

02:53.940 --> 02:55.410
A "super-sized Water Shuriken"?

02:55.410 --> 03:00.050
Also, this part of its head gets all spiky, like "ping"! It's so cool.

03:00.580 --> 03:01.230
"Ping"?

03:01.780 --> 03:04.450
I think it's kinda hard to understand with that explanation...

03:05.020 --> 03:06.760
You wanna see, Shota?

03:07.230 --> 03:08.990
Why don't you have a battle with my Gekkouga?

03:10.500 --> 03:12.270
Yes, please!

03:12.750 --> 03:15.330
Let us have a three-on-three battle, then.

03:16.930 --> 03:24.420
I want to test how much I've grown since our last battle by fighting under the same conditions as last time!

03:25.460 --> 03:26.640
Yeah, sure.

03:35.030 --> 03:35.680
In here, right?

03:36.020 --> 03:36.450
Yes.

03:47.990 --> 03:48.550
What's wrong?

03:54.230 --> 03:56.750
This is what we heard earlier!

03:57.120 --> 03:58.200
I wonder what that sound is.

04:01.590 --> 04:02.910
Isn't it coming closer?

04:08.520 --> 04:09.180
Did it stop?

04:16.730 --> 04:17.450
What <i>is</i> that?

04:20.600 --> 04:21.320
Everyone, run!

04:33.900 --> 04:34.600
Junsa-san!

04:57.110 --> 04:58.390
Checking for residual energy.

04:59.050 --> 05:02.890
The residual amount of the total output surpassed our initial anticipations by three units.

05:04.020 --> 05:06.940
It diverges from the expected output by about two percent.

05:07.430 --> 05:09.130
Both values are within our error range.

05:15.530 --> 05:16.660
Have any of the Cells been injured?

05:17.350 --> 05:18.040
None.

05:18.470 --> 05:20.680
Their level of exertion has decreased greatly as well.

05:21.290 --> 05:23.510
This result has surpassed our expectations by a lot.

05:28.430 --> 05:29.080
I see.

05:29.610 --> 05:30.880
Conduct further experiments.

05:31.490 --> 05:33.390
Get everything ready for us to proceed to the practical stage.

05:33.750 --> 05:34.800
Understood.

05:46.410 --> 05:48.780
You'll have to wait a bit for your turn.

05:51.360 --> 05:52.120
Please...

05:52.630 --> 05:53.780
Respond...

05:54.650 --> 05:55.340
What is the matter?

05:55.680 --> 05:56.570
Can you not hear us?

05:57.110 --> 05:58.310
Are you safe?

05:58.980 --> 06:00.200
Squishy!

06:01.470 --> 06:03.370
Did you hear? Satoshi and Shota are going to battle.

06:07.950 --> 06:08.750
What's the matter?

06:11.290 --> 06:12.760
You're worried about someone, huh?

06:14.970 --> 06:15.760
It'll be fine.

06:16.180 --> 06:17.410
We're here with you, right?

06:18.910 --> 06:26.390
When you and I have nuzzled,

06:26.890 --> 06:30.790
We're already friends

06:31.250 --> 06:34.880
We'll always be together!

06:35.330 --> 06:40.890
I'll protect you!

06:46.470 --> 06:47.690
What is this?

06:48.450 --> 06:49.950
A Battle Pulse Measuring Instrument.

06:50.710 --> 06:55.800
In order for Gekkouga to power up, Satoshi and Gekkouga's feelings need to synchronize.

06:56.340 --> 06:58.300
Wow, I see!

06:58.300 --> 06:59.510
All right, let's do this, shall we?

07:00.030 --> 07:00.560
Yes!

07:05.410 --> 07:06.490
My first will be Nidangill...

07:06.970 --> 07:07.600
I am counting on you!

07:11.990 --> 07:12.580
That's...

07:16.360 --> 07:19.780
Nidangill, the Sword Pokémon. The evolved form of Hitotsuki.

07:20.160 --> 07:24.060
The complex attack patterns of its two swords are said to be unstoppable,

07:24.060 --> 07:26.810
even for an opponent greatly accomplished at swordplay.

07:28.040 --> 07:30.410
So the Hitotsuki we battled earlier has evolved, huh?

07:32.130 --> 07:32.710
In that case...

07:33.850 --> 07:34.380
Onvern,

07:34.680 --> 07:35.590
I choose you!

07:41.280 --> 07:42.930
Your Pokémon has evolved too!

07:43.350 --> 07:45.270
Onvern looks cool!

07:45.460 --> 07:47.100
Yeah, it's become really strong!

07:51.170 --> 07:52.010
Let's go, Onvern!

07:52.340 --> 07:53.210
Acrobatics!

07:59.020 --> 08:00.300
Nidangill, Iron Defense!

08:05.960 --> 08:06.780
Let's attack.

08:07.000 --> 08:08.390
Use Acrobatics again!

08:11.540 --> 08:13.380
And you use Iron Defense again!

08:18.700 --> 08:19.880
It got blocked again!

08:21.630 --> 08:26.200
His strategy is to have Nidangill use Iron Defense to protect itself from attacks and tire the opponent out.

08:31.080 --> 08:31.590
This is our chance!

08:31.910 --> 08:33.760
Nidangill, use Slash, please!

08:41.980 --> 08:43.080
We will settle this with Night Slash!

08:53.890 --> 08:54.720
Dragon Claw!

08:59.960 --> 09:00.600
Nidangill!

09:01.070 --> 09:02.070
Acrobatics!

09:08.410 --> 09:09.130
Nidangill!

09:15.380 --> 09:15.940
All right!

09:17.510 --> 09:18.310
Nidangill,

09:18.870 --> 09:20.090
thank you very much.

09:20.790 --> 09:25.000
Even in the smoke, it had no trouble locating us.

09:25.650 --> 09:26.790
But how...?

09:27.450 --> 09:29.960
Onvern can use sound waves to locate its opponent.

09:31.810 --> 09:33.260
I see. So that is why...

09:34.160 --> 09:35.920
I have received some EXP.

09:36.440 --> 09:38.460
Shota, who will you use next?

09:39.170 --> 09:39.580
This one!

09:40.950 --> 09:41.850
I will count on you!

09:46.360 --> 09:47.050
What's that...?

09:49.920 --> 09:53.380
Bloster, the Launcher Pokémon. The evolved form of Udeppou.

09:54.100 --> 09:59.660
By expelling water from the nozzle in the back of its claw, it can move at a speed of 60 knots.

10:01.190 --> 10:02.030
A Bloster, huh?

10:02.650 --> 10:04.110
We will not lose this time.

10:04.510 --> 10:06.520
Bloster, Crabhammer!

10:09.800 --> 10:10.910
Dodge and use Boomburst!

10:20.620 --> 10:21.430
Calm down.

10:21.730 --> 10:22.750
Heal Pulse!

10:27.390 --> 10:28.390
It's all lively!

10:29.870 --> 10:32.540
Heal Pulse is a move that recovers stamina.

10:33.280 --> 10:37.520
The effect of Bloster's Ability, Mega Launcher, also contributed to it recovering substantially.

10:37.730 --> 10:38.580
No way!

10:39.110 --> 10:40.650
Onvern, Dragon Claw!

10:43.910 --> 10:45.530
Bloster, Dragon Pulse!

10:51.300 --> 10:52.000
Onvern!

11:00.210 --> 11:01.000
All right!

11:01.510 --> 11:02.790
Awesome!

11:02.790 --> 11:04.230
Was that also something its Ability did?

11:04.860 --> 11:07.640
All aura and pulse moves are powered up.

11:08.110 --> 11:09.250
Thank you, Onvern.

11:10.340 --> 11:11.470
That was a good battle.

11:12.870 --> 11:13.390
Luchabull,

11:13.760 --> 11:14.700
I choose you!

11:24.670 --> 11:25.810
Pokémon Quiz.

11:26.430 --> 11:27.320
The answer is...?

11:29.050 --> 11:38.920
Coming up next:

11:29.050 --> 11:34.020
The battle gets even more heated!

11:29.950 --> 11:34.690
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

11:34.080 --> 11:38.920
Gekkouga VS Jukain!!

11:48.610 --> 11:49.760
Dragon Pulse!

11:49.760 --> 11:50.350
Dodge!

11:53.060 --> 11:54.950
I don't know how this Mega Launcher or whatever works, but...

11:55.240 --> 11:56.690
...how's this?!

11:57.750 --> 11:58.710
Restrain its pincers!

12:01.670 --> 12:03.860
Satoshi, I knew you would do that!

12:04.280 --> 12:06.550
Bloster, fire Dragon Pulse against the ground!

12:10.480 --> 12:11.580
No way! It's flying!

12:11.970 --> 12:13.830
You wanna have a mid-air fight, huh?

12:14.360 --> 12:16.080
Luchabull, go higher!

12:19.710 --> 12:20.670
Flying Press!

12:22.840 --> 12:23.400
Let it come closer!

12:25.030 --> 12:26.670
Now, use Ice Beam!

12:31.530 --> 12:32.310
Luchabull!

12:33.670 --> 12:34.910
He planned this!

12:35.130 --> 12:37.180
That is super effective against Luchabull!

12:43.390 --> 12:44.530
Thank you, Luchabull.

12:44.950 --> 12:46.000
Take a long rest.

12:46.860 --> 12:48.370
I was so focused on pulse moves...

12:48.890 --> 12:50.570
...that I didn't even think of the possibility that you'd use Ice Beam.

12:51.150 --> 12:54.150
I had it learn that because it is weak against Grass types,

12:54.650 --> 12:55.680
and it seems it was a good idea.

12:56.870 --> 13:00.070
He used Dragon Pulse not to attack but to escape,

13:00.660 --> 13:03.820
and then finished the match with Ice Beam, a move Luchabull is weak against.

13:04.560 --> 13:06.970
He puts a lot of care into how he puts moves together.

13:07.420 --> 13:09.170
Shota is eager to study, after all.

13:09.620 --> 13:11.380
His efforts must have taken shape.

13:12.070 --> 13:14.490
It is no wonder that he was able to get eight badges.

13:15.780 --> 13:16.460
He's right...

13:16.960 --> 13:19.320
Shota's become so strong I barely recognize him.

13:20.290 --> 13:21.790
We can't afford to be careless.

13:22.410 --> 13:24.530
Gekkouga, it's finally your turn!

13:29.030 --> 13:30.070
Gekkouga...

13:30.610 --> 13:32.600
We are bound to receive quite a bit of EXP from that!

13:33.190 --> 13:33.940
Let us do our best!

13:34.650 --> 13:36.580
Bloster, Dragon Pulse!

13:38.880 --> 13:39.440
Dodge!

13:42.690 --> 13:43.090
It is fast!

13:43.840 --> 13:44.760
What do we do next?

13:45.210 --> 13:45.940
Should we keep going like this?

13:46.410 --> 13:47.550
What will Shota use?

13:50.730 --> 13:52.340
Bloster, Ice Beam!

13:52.660 --> 13:53.280
Gekkouga!

13:53.580 --> 13:54.560
Use Cut!

14:07.080 --> 14:07.900
Bloster!

14:08.490 --> 14:10.840
It's strong, it's fast, it's cool!

14:12.470 --> 14:13.530
Citron, how does it look?

14:14.100 --> 14:16.500
Their battle pulses are unchanged and are running parallel.

14:17.030 --> 14:19.550
They are not moving like they were during the battle with Carne-san.

14:20.230 --> 14:21.210
I wonder what's wrong.

14:22.420 --> 14:24.130
Thank you for your hard work, Bloster.

14:24.930 --> 14:26.370
Please leave the rest to us.

14:29.260 --> 14:30.890
I am counting on you, Jukain!

14:35.820 --> 14:37.220
It's time, Shota.

14:37.670 --> 14:40.200
I will fight with the intention of showing you signs of my growth.

14:40.790 --> 14:42.060
I will give it all I got!

14:42.850 --> 14:44.390
All right, this is where it starts.

14:45.090 --> 14:46.640
We have collected eight badges,

14:47.370 --> 14:47.810
but...

14:48.480 --> 14:49.380
...this is Satoshi.

14:50.090 --> 14:51.430
We have to beat Satoshi.

14:52.730 --> 14:54.690
As proof that I have grown up,

14:55.420 --> 14:56.890
I want Satoshi to approve of me.

14:58.020 --> 15:01.010
I will prove myself by defeating Satoshi.

15:01.400 --> 15:02.740
Let us begin, Jukain!

15:02.740 --> 15:03.580
Leaf Blade!

15:06.590 --> 15:08.650
Let's show them our power.

15:09.390 --> 15:10.360
Go, Gekkouga!

15:10.850 --> 15:11.860
Aerial Ace!

15:21.710 --> 15:22.570
Bullet Seed!

15:23.960 --> 15:25.000
Water Shuriken!

15:29.620 --> 15:30.320
Leaf Blade!

15:32.880 --> 15:33.690
Double Team!

15:36.640 --> 15:37.190
Chase after them!

15:37.420 --> 15:38.690
Leaf Blade!

15:44.750 --> 15:45.210
It's fast!

15:45.760 --> 15:48.370
Now it is attempting a close-range fight, something that Gekkouga specializes in.

15:48.800 --> 15:49.340
Gekkouga,

15:49.630 --> 15:50.460
Cut!

15:52.450 --> 15:52.910
Step back!

15:55.920 --> 15:57.070
Leaf Storm!

16:05.200 --> 16:05.750
What?!

16:09.440 --> 16:10.770
Now it moved away from it?

16:11.370 --> 16:13.820
The way he makes use of short and long distances is outstanding.

16:14.230 --> 16:15.350
Get up, Gekkouga!

16:20.230 --> 16:21.270
You're good, Shota.

16:22.290 --> 16:23.970
There are things you don't notice about a person unless you fight them.

16:24.650 --> 16:24.910
Shota...

16:25.790 --> 16:27.120
You've really become strong.

16:28.200 --> 16:30.920
You must have trained and worked incredibly hard to achieve that.

16:31.700 --> 16:32.220
Otherwise...

16:32.700 --> 16:34.030
...you couldn't have become this strong in such a short time...

16:35.040 --> 16:36.690
Being able to handle any type of situation...

16:37.190 --> 16:38.970
...and selecting the optimal moves.

16:40.110 --> 16:42.070
That is also something I learned from Satoshi.

16:43.360 --> 16:44.890
He really surprised me.

16:45.350 --> 16:45.940
Gekkouga,

16:46.170 --> 16:47.070
Aerial Ace!

16:48.570 --> 16:49.040
Here it comes.

17:03.310 --> 17:05.030
Let's go, Gekkouga!

17:05.680 --> 17:08.710
We'll become one!

17:25.800 --> 17:26.520
...We can't?

17:30.390 --> 17:31.710
Their battle pulses are...

17:32.220 --> 17:33.020
...moving apart.

17:33.350 --> 17:33.830
Huh?

17:35.850 --> 17:36.150
Huh?

17:36.710 --> 17:38.990
How did we make it happen again?

17:41.790 --> 17:43.810
Jukain, Leaf Storm!

17:51.600 --> 17:52.400
Gekkouga!

17:54.290 --> 17:55.740
Let us settle this with Leaf Blade!

18:17.480 --> 18:18.830
Gekkouga, hang in there!

18:24.020 --> 18:24.850
We lost.

18:26.680 --> 18:27.600
We defeated...

18:28.300 --> 18:29.140
...Gekkouga...

18:31.160 --> 18:33.700
We won! We won against Satoshi!

18:35.520 --> 18:36.940
Satoshi lost...

18:37.170 --> 18:38.790
It happens.

18:39.320 --> 18:41.430
Keeping up a winning streak is next to impossible.

18:41.820 --> 18:43.830
Shota has become really strong, though.

18:44.360 --> 18:44.760
He has.

18:45.310 --> 18:48.930
I can only imagine how hard he worked during this short time period.

18:49.530 --> 18:51.080
Gekkouga, please return.

18:58.820 --> 19:00.150
Man, he got me.

19:02.720 --> 19:03.390
Satoshi,

19:04.560 --> 19:06.470
I have become strong, have I not?

19:06.770 --> 19:07.160
Yeah,

19:07.890 --> 19:09.120
<i>amazingly </i>strong.

19:09.960 --> 19:11.120
You surprised me.

19:22.630 --> 19:25.070
I wonder why we were unable to power up today.

19:25.450 --> 19:27.090
I do not know the reason, but...

19:27.690 --> 19:31.600
...in this battle, your battle pulses did not overlap at all.

19:34.230 --> 19:35.380
...Okay, this isn't working.

19:35.930 --> 19:37.600
Brooding over it won't help!

19:38.460 --> 19:41.360
It won't go like this next time, Shota!

19:43.450 --> 19:43.960
Sure!

19:44.940 --> 19:47.490
All right, let's set off to Eisetsu City!

19:49.780 --> 19:51.160
Can I come with you?

19:51.510 --> 19:54.040
I would love to observe your battle, Satoshi!

19:54.650 --> 19:57.600
Yeah, I'll make sure to get my eighth badge.

19:58.070 --> 19:58.700
Watch us!

20:05.930 --> 20:06.970
Wow!

20:07.900 --> 20:08.670
Whoa!

20:08.670 --> 20:10.740
I can see Eisetsu City!

20:13.570 --> 20:16.710
Satoshi and his friends have finally arrived in Eisetsu City.

20:17.740 --> 20:22.550
At last, the final Gym match, where Satoshi aims to get his eighth badge, begins.

20:28.860 --> 20:30.950
PokéLove TV!

20:31.360 --> 20:33.370
All right, it's started! Brought to you by me, Ken, and...

20:33.370 --> 20:35.270
Hi! I'm Jenny, nice to meet you!

20:35.270 --> 20:37.020
Today we will introduce Juptile!

20:37.220 --> 20:39.600
There are leaves on its arms. I should go pick them off for it!

20:39.600 --> 20:43.760
No, no! The attacks it delivers from those leaves are extremely sharp!

20:43.760 --> 20:45.040
What?!

20:45.380 --> 20:46.130
I've decided!

20:46.130 --> 20:46.890
Oh, what is it?

20:47.160 --> 20:49.820
I was thinking about having Juptile make my garden pretty!

20:49.820 --> 20:52.570
Mow your lawn yourself!

20:54.610 --> 20:57.050
Whoa, that's its evolved form Jukain!

20:57.250 --> 21:01.360
Once it turns into a Jukain, the leaves on its arms become sharper and can slice down thick trees!

21:01.360 --> 21:03.090
Awesome!

21:03.090 --> 21:04.620
Oh, I've got a nice idea.

21:04.620 --> 21:05.540
What is it?

21:05.920 --> 21:07.290
Time to transform!

21:14.470 --> 21:15.210
What do you think?

21:15.640 --> 21:17.640
I'll hold a samba carnival with Jukain!

21:17.840 --> 21:20.480
Oh my god!

21:20.960 --> 21:25.970
Pokémon no Uchi Atsumaru?

21:20.960 --> 21:25.970
Sunday May 15th at 8am!

21:20.960 --> 21:22.940
Trendy Angel show up!

21:21.920 --> 21:22.940
Pe-pe-peh!

21:22.940 --> 21:25.970
Miyu Honda

21:22.940 --> 21:25.970
Nobunari Oda

21:23.790 --> 21:24.890
On Sunday at 8am!

21:28.290 --> 21:30.210
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.360 --> 21:31.450
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.410 --> 21:33.780
It's time for my final Gym match!

